
/*!
	add counter representing how many clients use an extension.

	unloading should happen per client close. the client loads, the counter goes up, the counter goes down on client close. if 0, unload.
*/

/*!
	max client amount?
*/

/*!
	when request comes in, event must be handled before a reply, synchronously. that is slow, maybe reform to send events at the same time, even if the design is weird.
*/

/*!
	keep replies lossless and events lossy. if the buffer fills up, lose events but do not lose replies.
*/

/*!
	support client id XOR with /dev/urandom for obfuscation.
*/

/*!
	support extension id XOR with /dev/urandom for obfuscation.
*/

/*!
	keep track of base events per extension to avoid holes, if you care. adding extensions should probably not be allowed after a little bit since the start anyway.

	same goes for loading and unloading extensions if unloading is at all possible.
*/

/*!
	introduce stacks to store clients, extensions etc in holes left behind by removals.
*/



























